# The filesystem registry: which filesystem service handles which partition
# type, as *data* (specs/services.md). Adding a filesystem is adding a row here
# and a binary to the image -- not a code change -- and the day the same file
# comes from a volume instead of the initrd, only its source changes.
#
# One row per partition type, key=value fields:
#   type    the GPT partition type GUID, canonical form (the on-disk entry is
#           the usual mixed-endian layout; the parser reads the canonical text)
#   kind    the instance-name prefix a started service wears: a partition on
#           BD0 with this kind is fat.BD0Part0, and the VFS sees the volume's
#           own label, not the instance name
#   binary  the initrd entry the service starts from
#
# A partition whose type is not here is reported and not started: a filesystem
# is a decision the disk makes, and an unknown one is refused loudly rather
# than guessed at.

# The Aegir system volume (specs/services.md). It wears the system GUID, and
# the system stands on it; FAT is its filesystem until the BFS migration arc
# moves it, and this row is what moves with it.
type=5cd58811-9bf5-4af3-8682-9b76edce3535 kind=fat binary=aegir-fs-fat

# Microsoft basic data: the type a FAT partition on GPT carries, and what the
# test disk's interchange volumes are (specs/fat.md).
type=ebd0a0a2-b9e5-4433-87c0-68b6b72699c7 kind=fat binary=aegir-fs-fat

# The Be File System (specs/bfs.md): Aegir's own filesystem, and the one the
# system volume migrates to. The GUID is BFS's on GPT.
type=42465331-3ba3-10f1-802a-4861696b7521 kind=bfs binary=aegir-fs-bfs
